Notebook[
 {Cell["How the four-loop No-Crown hidden-region audits were performed", 
   "Title"], 
  Cell[
   "A reproducible guide to the wide-angle and three-channel Regge searches", 
   "Subtitle"], Cell["Purpose. The two detailed audit notebooks contain a \
large amount of run history and diagnostic output. This notebook instead \
presents the mathematical question, one ordinary HRF run, the enumeration of \
graphs and contraction strata, and the exact shortcuts that made the \
exhaustive parts feasible. It is intended to be sufficiently precise that the \
strategy can be reimplemented independently.", "Text"], 
  CellGroupData[{Cell["1. Question, sample and exact scope", "Section"], 
    Cell["The sample consists of sixteen massless four-loop 2->2 graphs. Each \
graph has mixed-sign Schwinger-parameter derivatives, so the elementary \
necessary test for a cancellation pinch does not exclude it. None contains \
the three-loop Crown as a contraction minor. The question is whether any \
graph, in its interior or on a contraction boundary, has a hidden region at \
wide angle or in one of the three Regge channels.", "Text"], 
    Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"audit\"", "\"cases\"", "\"HR found\"", 
          "\"unresolved\"", "\"logical status\""}, 
         {"\"wide angle: interiors plus all nonempty boundaries\"", "114468", 
          "0", "0", "\"complete\""}, {"\"Regge: interiors\"", "48", "0", "0", 
          "\"complete\""}, {"\"Regge: nonempty boundaries\"", "343356", "0", 
          "0", "\"complete\""}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, 
        AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxBackground -> {"Columns" -> {{None}}, 
          "Rows" -> {GrayLevel[0.85], None}}, GridBoxFrame -> 
         {"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}, GridBoxItemSize -> 
         {"Columns" -> {Automatic, Automatic}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
        BaseStyle -> {FontSize -> 11}], "Grid"]], "Output"], 
    Cell["Both conclusions are now exhaustive for this sample. At wide angle \
the earlier record covered the 188 codimension-two strata containing x8; the \
current generator-first run separately certifies all 1012 complementary \
strata. Keeping those provenances distinct makes clear which conclusions come \
from the historical scan and which come from the present exact rerun.", 
     "Text"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"stratum\"", "\"number\"", 
          "\"wide-angle stored coverage\"", "\"Regge coverage\""}, 
         {"\"interior\"", "16", "\"all 16\"", 
          "\"48 graph/channel interiors\""}, {"\"codimension 1\"", "204", 
          "\"all 204\"", "\"all\""}, {"\"codimension 2\"", "1200", 
          "\"188 legacy x8 strata plus 1012 current complementary strata\"", 
          "\"all\""}, {"\"codimension 3\"", "4312", "\"all 4312\"", 
          "\"all\""}, {"\"codimension 4 through E-2\"", "108736", 
          "\"all 108736\"", "\"all\""}, {"\"all nonempty boundaries\"", 
          "114452", "\"all 114452\"", "\"114452 per channel\""}}, 
        GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, AutoDelete -> False, 
        GridBoxBackground -> {"Columns" -> {{None}}, 
          "Rows" -> {GrayLevel[0.85], None}}, GridBoxFrame -> 
         {"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}, GridBoxItemSize -> 
         {"Columns" -> {Automatic, Automatic}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
        BaseStyle -> {FontSize -> 11}], "Grid"]], "Output"]}, Open], 
  CellGroupData[{Cell["2. The HRF decision problem on one stratum", 
     "Section"], Cell["Fix a graph, a kinematic limit and a contraction set \
S. Set x_i=0 for i in S and keep all remaining Schwinger parameters positive. \
In ordinary wide-angle scattering the native leading polynomial F0 is already \
the correct starting point; no preliminary face selection is required.", 
     "Text"], Cell["HRF first factorises the mixed-sign derivatives of F0 and \
identifies compatible polynomial cancellation factors. Admissible products of \
these factors define candidate generators of the cancellation ideal. Only \
then does HRF construct decompositions F0=F_SL+F_obs in which F_SL belongs to \
that ideal. Finally it solves for a scaling vector rho which makes F_SL \
homogeneous and places F_obs, U and every restored delta layer at strictly \
higher weight.", "Text"], 
    Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"condition\"", "\"equation tested\"", 
          "\"meaning\""}, {"\"positive pinch\"", "\"d_i F_SL=0, x_i>0\"", 
          "\"first-sheet Landau stationary point on the active stratum\""}, 
         {"\"face homogeneity\"", "\"rho.(r_a-r_b)=0 for a,b in F_SL\"", 
          "\"the proposed superleading monomials scale together\""}, 
         {"\"strict hierarchy\"", "\"rho.(r_c-r_a)+eta_c-eta_a>0\"", "\"all \
complementary and restored-layer monomials are genuinely later\""}}, 
        GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, AutoDelete -> False, 
        GridBoxBackground -> {"Columns" -> {{None}}, 
          "Rows" -> {GrayLevel[0.85], None}}, GridBoxFrame -> 
         {"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}, GridBoxItemSize -> 
         {"Columns" -> {Automatic, Automatic}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
        BaseStyle -> {FontSize -> 11}], "Grid"]], "Output"], 
    Cell["The positive pinch is tested on the isolated F_SL, not on the \
unscaled F0. If a scaling solution exists, the monomials of F_SL necessarily \
form the corresponding lower face after that scaling has been found. This \
geometric statement certifies the result; it is not the candidate-generation \
step for an ordinary wide-angle run.", "Text"]}, Open], 
  CellGroupData[{Cell["3. One ordinary HRF run", "Section"], 
    Cell["The executable cell below runs only the interior of the first \
diagram (85774). Its purpose is to display one complete HRF decision with all \
certification settings exposed; it does not rerun the full sixteen-graph \
boundary audit. The exhaustive audit is represented later by its compact \
persisted certificates. The historical discovery runner used a candidate \
limit of 128; for a new absence claim, the explicit unbounded settings below \
are preferable.", "Text"], 
    Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"setting\"", "\"certification value\"", 
          "\"reason\""}, {"\"GeneratorMode\"", "\"PairSectors\"", 
          "\"allow the two kinematic sectors of wide-angle 2->2 scattering\""}\
, {"\"MaxGenerators\"", "2", 
          "\"one cancellation generator per sector is sufficient for this run \
mode\""}, {"\"UseExtendedFactors\"", "True", 
          "\"include polynomial, not only binomial, cancellation factors\""}, 
         {"\"EnableSignedMonomialPairs\"", "False", 
          "\"use factors of complete derivatives and channel polynomials\""}, 
         {"\"StopOnFirstAdmissible\"", "False", 
          "\"retain every admissible obstruction presentation\""}, 
         {"\"CandidateGeneratorSetLimit\"", "\[Infinity]", 
          "\"a finite value can find a witness but cannot prove absence\""}, 
         {"\"MaxTwoGeneratorUnionTrials\"", "\[Infinity]", 
          "\"do not truncate two-sector unions\""}, 
         {"\"PolynomialMaxMonomials\"", "Automatic", "\"derive the complete \
factor size from the polynomial being audited\""}, 
         {"\"CoverageScalingMethod\"", "\"ExactCoverage\"", 
          "\"solve the homogeneous face and strict hierarchy together\""}, 
         {"\"RequireValidScalingForHiddenRegionQ\"", "True", "\"a \
cancellation candidate without a positive hierarchy gap is not an HR\""}}, 
        GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, AutoDelete -> False, 
        GridBoxBackground -> {"Columns" -> {{None}}, 
          "Rows" -> {GrayLevel[0.85], None}}, GridBoxFrame -> 
         {"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}, GridBoxItemSize -> 
         {"Columns" -> {Automatic, Automatic}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
        BaseStyle -> {FontSize -> 11}], "Grid"]], "Output"], 
    Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"SetDirectory", "[", 
          RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], "]"}], ";", 
        RowBox[{"$HRFRunWideAngle16NoCrownAuditOnLoad", "=", "False"}], ";", 
        RowBox[{"<<", "\"HRF_WideAngle16NoCrownAudit.wl\""}], ";", 
        RowBox[{"rec", "=", RowBox[{"First", "[", 
            RowBox[{"hrfWA16LoadRecords", "[", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
        RowBox[{"zero", "=", RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], ";", 
        RowBox[{"f", "=", RowBox[{"Expand", "[", RowBox[
             {RowBox[{"rec", "[", "\"F0\"", "]"}], "/.", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
              RowBox[{"Thread", "[", RowBox[{"zero", "\[Rule]", "0"}], 
                "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"u", "=", 
          RowBox[{"Expand", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"rec", "[", "\"U\"", "]"}], 
              "/.", "\[VeryThinSpace]", RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
                RowBox[{"zero", "\[Rule]", "0"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
        RowBox[{"fFull", "=", RowBox[{"Expand", "[", 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"rec", "[", "\"Data\"", "]"}], "[", 
                "\"FOnShell\"", "]"}], "/.", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
              RowBox[{"Thread", "[", RowBox[{"zero", "\[Rule]", "0"}], 
                "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"vars", "=", 
          RowBox[{"Complement", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"rec", "[", "\"Vars\"", 
                "]"}], ",", "zero"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
        RowBox[{"scan", "=", RowBox[{"findObstructions", "[", 
            RowBox[{"f", ",", "vars", ",", "KinAssump4ptOnShell", ",", 
              "KinVars4pt", ",", "20", ",", RowBox[{"\"UseExtendedFactors\"", 
                "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"GeneratorMode\"", 
                "\[Rule]", "\"PairSectors\""}], ",", RowBox[{
                "\"MaxGenerators\"", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"\"EnableSignedMonomialPairs\"", "\[Rule]", "False"}], 
              ",", RowBox[{"\"StopOnFirstAdmissible\"", "\[Rule]", "False"}], 
              ",", RowBox[{"\"CandidateGeneratorSetLimit\"", "\[Rule]", 
                "\[Infinity]"}], ",", RowBox[{
                "\"MaxTwoGeneratorUnionTrials\"", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}], 
              ",", RowBox[{"\"PolynomialMaxMonomials\"", "\[Rule]", 
                "Automatic"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"StoreAllObstructionTrialsQ\"", 
                "\[Rule]", "False"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"U\"", "\[Rule]", "u"}], 
              ",", RowBox[{"\"FObsForScaling\"", "\[Rule]", RowBox[
                 {"Association", "[", RowBox[{"\"DeltaLayers\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    RowBox[{"hrfDeltaLayerAssociation", "[", RowBox[{"fFull", 
                        ",", "\[Delta]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"\"CoverageScalingMethod\"", "\[Rule]", 
                "\"ExactCoverage\""}], ",", RowBox[{
                "\"RequireValidScalingForHiddenRegionQ\"", "\[Rule]", 
                "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"Association", "[", 
          RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"DiagramID\"", "\[Rule]", RowBox[{"rec", "[", 
                "\"ID\"", "]"}]}], ",", RowBox[{"\"ContractedVariables\"", 
              "\[Rule]", "zero"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"Stratum\"", "\[Rule]", 
              RowBox[{"If", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"zero", "===", RowBox[
                     {"{", "}"}]}], ",", "\"interior\"", ",", 
                  "\"boundary\""}], "]"}]}], ",", RowBox[{"\"Conclusion\"", 
              "\[Rule]", RowBox[{"Which", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"TrueQ", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"scan", "[", "\"HiddenRegionQ\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
                  ",", "\"hidden region found\"", ",", RowBox[
                   {RowBox[{"TrueQ", "[", RowBox[{"scan", "[", 
                        "\"HiddenRegionSearchCompleteQ\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
                    "&&", RowBox[{"!", RowBox[{"TrueQ", "[", RowBox[{"scan", 
                          "[", "\"SearchTruncatedQ\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
                  "\"complete search: no hidden region\"", ",", "True", ",", 
                  "\"unresolved\""}], "]"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"HiddenRegionCount\"", "\[Rule]", RowBox[{"scan", "[", 
                "\"HiddenRegionCount\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"CandidateGeneratorCount\"", "\[Rule]", 
              RowBox[{"scan", "[", "\"CandidateGeneratorCount\"", "]"}]}], 
            ",", RowBox[{"\"ValidObstructionTrialCount\"", "\[Rule]", 
              RowBox[{"scan", "[", "\"ValidObstructionTrialCount\"", "]"}]}], 
            ",", RowBox[{"\"SearchTruncatedQ\"", "\[Rule]", RowBox[{"scan", 
                "[", "\"SearchTruncatedQ\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"HiddenRegionSearchCompleteQ\"", "\[Rule]", 
              RowBox[{"scan", "[", "\"HiddenRegionSearchCompleteQ\"", 
                "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input"], Cell["The final association is \
deliberately short. Conclusion equal to \"complete search: no hidden region\" \
means that the candidate construction and all required decisions completed \
without truncation. \"Unresolved\" must not be read as NoHR.", "Text"], 
    Cell["A negative row is reportable only when SearchTruncatedQ is False \
and all positivity and scaling solves are resolved. A positive witness can be \
found with finite budgets, but a finite budget cannot certify that no \
unvisited generator set works.", "Text"], Cell["For the sixteen interiors, \
the stored scan tried PairSectors, Adaptive and SingleProduct modes. The \
current complete polynomial-factor construction produces no admissible \
generator in any interior. The later exposed-face calculation was introduced \
historically as an independent safeguard when the completeness of the factor \
harvest was still in question; it is not the preferred HRF workflow after \
removal of the hard caps.", "Text"]}, Open], 
  CellGroupData[{Cell["4. Enumerating graphs and contraction boundaries", 
     "Section"], Cell["The ordered internal-edge list fixes the \
correspondence x0,x1,... . A boundary stratum is a subset S of these \
variables, imposed by x_i=0 for i in S. For a graph with E internal edges, \
codimension k contains Binomial[E,k] strata. The scan stops at k=E-2 because \
fewer than two active Schwinger parameters cannot support a nontrivial \
cancellation hypersurface.", "Text"], 
    Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"zeroSets", "[", 
          RowBox[{"rec_", ",", "k_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
        RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"rec", "[", "\"Vars\"", 
              "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "k", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input"], 
    Cell["Four graphs have E=12 and twelve have E=13. This gives the counts \
in Section 1. Graph identity or crossing was used to reduce work only after \
an explicit variable permutation was shown to transport every polynomial \
entering the decision problem.", "Text"], 
    Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"diagram\"", "\"E\"", 
          "\"ordered internal edges (x0,x1,...)\"", 
          "\"external attachments\""}, {"85774", "12", 
          RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"0\"", ",", 
                  RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"0\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[
                     {"1", ",", "5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"\"0\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"0\"", ",", 
